From a154f5382451f98f1ef844336e3b5111c3f9fe5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 04:47:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] klzh2: the encoder picks a chunk's table by estimate
 before coding, heap for the count scaling

A short code chunk was coded twice (own table, predefined table) and a short literal chunk
three times (khuf, tANS) to keep the smallest. kza_plan now gives the estimated size of
each choice from the scaled counts (integers), and only the cheaper is coded; literal tANS
is tried only when its estimate is under khuf's actual size. kza_normalize moved one state
per pass over all symbols: O(states moved x symbols), the bulk of the encoder's time on 4 KiB
blocks of binary data; the same choice now comes from a binary heap keyed by (cost, symbol).
Format unchanged; frozen frames still decode. natbench, 4 KiB blocks of xml+dickens+osdb,
k2h1: 13,986,727 -> 13,986,796 bytes; compress speed in results (indicative).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FUEN4aRWhUw7yL7cZMqTmZ
---
